        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-23T04:18:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If column is not found, do we want to throw IIlegalArgumentException or just return it silently?\nIt looks like we have different way to handle it between this line and getXyz functions below.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 248,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 248,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "10c1a6789d65a399f19023906e737826cdaa9156",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3caf674a_2ed34eda",
        "filename": "services/ipmemorystore/java/com/android/server/net/ipmemorystore/IpMemoryStoreDatabase.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-23T07:43:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Generally speaking if the column is not found the memory store is completely busted.\nBut you have a point, we should handle it here in the same ways as other places, and in other places the policy is : let\u0027s not crash even if the memory store is busted.\nDone.",
      "parentUuid": "548c5c09_85fcf531",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 248,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 248,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "10c1a6789d65a399f19023906e737826cdaa9156",
