    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ccf8643_2f7a6444",
        "filename": "services/ipmemorystore/java/com/android/server/net/ipmemorystore/IpMemoryStoreDatabase.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 456,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-23T04:18:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Understand that we need to cut down the number of lines to search.\nBut just curious that: do we have any case that we don\u0027t have any field equals but closeness is high?",
      "revId": "10c1a6789d65a399f19023906e737826cdaa9156",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86e2d4f5_88b80bee",
        "filename": "services/ipmemorystore/java/com/android/server/net/ipmemorystore/IpMemoryStoreDatabase.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 456,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-23T07:43:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No. The closeness is determined by how many fields are equal, so if no field is equal there is exactly zero chance of that line being group-close. Therefore this only ever drops lines that are guaranteed not to match.",
      "parentUuid": "7ccf8643_2f7a6444",
      "revId": "10c1a6789d65a399f19023906e737826cdaa9156",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
